<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seventh-day Adventist Church</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Seventh-day Adventism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Seventh-day Adventist Church is a Protestant Christian denomination formally organised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1863, which keeps Saturday as the Sabbath and emphasises the imminent Second Coming of Christ. It grew through missions into a worldwide church with millions of members, running schools and hospitals. The people of Pitcairn Island converted to it after an Adventist missionary's visit in 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seventh-day-adventist-church.jpg" alt="Seventh-day Adventist Church" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adventist_Symbol.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
